From: postmarketOS chopin bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] mali: enable implicit dma-buf fences for native DRM sharing

Native userspace submits imported GEM dma-bufs as external resources. Without
MALI_DMA_FENCE, those GPU jobs neither publish producer fences nor wait for
other drivers' accesses. Poll then reports a buffer readable while its GPU
writer is still pending.

The MediaTek in-tree build bypasses Mali's Kconfig. Enable both the Kbuild
objects and the matching preprocessor definition in its existing custom
environment; leave the driver's explicit Android-fence opt-out unchanged.

--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/gpu/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild-mtk-custom-env
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/gpu/gpu_mali/mali_valhall/mali-r32p1/drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/Kbuild-mtk-custom-env
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@
 # build support for a ARM Mali Midgard GPU
 CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD := y
 
+# Native DRM sharing uses dma-buf reservation fences.
+CONFIG_MALI_DMA_FENCE := y
+ccflags-y += -DCONFIG_MALI_DMA_FENCE=1
+
 # use mtk platform
 CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_THIRDPARTY := y
 ifeq ($(CONFIG_MACH_MT6833),y)
